@1 = ~Why do you bother me?~
@2 = ~Whoah. Sorry. Didn't mean to poke the bear.~
@3 = ~I am not intruding am I? This is an open space after all.~
@4 = ~Uh... my apologies. I didn't mean to lash out at you. I am dealing with an issue of... spectacular grandeur, so to speak.~
@5 = ~Uh... no. No, no, of course not. Pardon my manners. I did not mean to come off as rude. I am dealing with an issue of... spectacular grandeur, so to speak.~
@6 = ~It seems Tymora's luck shines on you. We are dealing with such problems recently. We might be able to help if you tell us more.~
@7 = ~If you are so inclined to tell us more. We might be interested if there is a reward involved. Monetary reward.~
@8 = ~Well. Good luck dealing with your problem.~
@9 = ~Well, I suppose it won't hurt to share my story. My name is Alphyra La Bastica, from Calimshan. I travelled all the way here to find a mage skilled enough to help me lift a powerful curse that was cast upon me. Curse of the White Flame.~
@10 = ~Me and my... lover were trying to push things one step further. Pers was trying to propose to me...~
@11 = ~(Keep listening)~
@12 = ~Let me guess. Your lover turned out to be evil, and gave you a cursed ring so you never leave him again.~
@13 = ~What? Why would that be the first thing to come to your mind? Listen, and do not cut in.~
@14 = ~Pers bought a beautiful ring from an enigmatic peddler for me, and presented it to me as a token of his love and loyalty. I knew something felt off, but I was too blinded by my excitement and joy at that moment. He put it on my finger, and since then I've been having… strange dreams.~
@15 = ~These dreams felt… like memories. Memories that don't belong to me. Almost as if I saw events unfolding before me through another person's eyes. It felt so vivid. I sought help of a proficient arcane master that lived near us, and asked him to identify the ring. It turned out it contains a magical curse called 'White Flame'.~
@16 = ~According to the legend, a soul of a powerful Djinni called Eleastrath was imprisoned within the ring during Spellplague. He attempted to cast a spell, but since world was devastated by wild magic and spellcasting was dangerous, he overestimated his own capabilities and trapped himself inside a once non-magical ring. Allegedly, magical mutation is so warped, that not even Elminster himself could release the Djinni or remove the curse. The peddler either didn't realise what kind of artifact he was selling or… he did it on purpose.~
@17 = ~I tried to get rid of the ring, but it always comes back. And worst of all, taking it off didn't help. These visions appear in my dreams every time I close my eyes. It's becoming insufferable.~
@18 = ~I see. What could we do to help?~
@19 = ~Edwin, do you have any advice?~
@20 = ~Dynaheir, can you possibly do something about it?~
@21 = ~I don't think I can help you. Good luck.~
@22 = ~I was told by Tim - a close relative of mine, about a mage that lives in Baldur's Gate somewhere. Unfortunately, I do not know his name. Tim once said this mage is capable of removing really sophisticated curses connected to wild magic. He has got some sort of device that allows to identify and possibly dispel such curses. Unfortunately, last time I tried to get to the city I was stopped by Flaming Fist officer who refused me entry due to increasing bandit population nearby. Even if I did gain access, I do not know who am I searching for. Or where. Do me a favour and try to ask around within the city. Maybe you'll find whoever it might be.~
@23 = ~I am not familiar with majority of rare spell mutation cases such as this, nor do I have the means of removing one but if my memory serves, Halbazzer Drin from Baldur's Gate has a special device for such instances. I surmise he shall ask for payment for such a service and losing money on such unimportant issue would not benefit our cause.~
@24 = ~Hm… I shan't make any guesses or false assumptions but I can tell thy this. A mage of powerful renown lives within Baldur's Gate city and owns a shop called Sorcerous Sundries. I do not recall the name, but I am fairly certain he has got a device that simplifies curse handling. He may be able to help.~
@25 = ~Did you find a mage?~
@26 = ~Yes. Halbazzer Drin from Baldur's Gate cast a spell using his special device for curse handling. You should be free of the curse now.~
@27 = ~No, still looking.~
@28 = ~Really? This is astonishing. Thank you so much for all the help. Most travellers would not want to waste time on stranger's trouble. Here, take this 200 gold coins and a wand of the heavens.~
@29 = ~We heard you have a vastly sufficient magical prowess. We seek help of someone who can deal with archaic curses. More specifically 'Curse of a White Flame'.~
@30 = ~Curse of a White Flame? I have heard of such a curse while studying magic tomes in my youth. I do have a potential way to dispel it but I won't do so for free, especially since it's not a life threatening curse. I will cast a spell using my special artifact, but... I need payment first. 5000 gold coins. I also need a name and location of whoever is afflicted by the curse.~
@31 = ~Here is 5000 gold coins. The victim is named Alphyra and she resides in Friendly Arm Inn.~
@32 = ~5000 gold coins is a bit too much. Maybe later.~
@33 = ~Alphyra~
@34 = ~Friendly Arm Inn~

@35 = ~Alphyra La Bastica has asked us to find a mage in Baldur's Gate who can remove the Curse of the White Flame afflicting her. She was told that such a mage may possess a device capable of identifying and dispelling rare curses caused by wild magic.~
@36 = ~Alphyra is free of the Curse of the White Flame. Halbazzer Drin has removed the curse using his special device.~

@37 = ~Be on your way then. By the time you make it to Friendly Arm Inn, she should be free of the curse.~

@38 = ~The Curse of the White Flame~
@39 = ~I found Halbazzer Drin in Baldur's Gate and paid him 5,000 gold to lift Alphyra's curse. He assured me she would be free by the time I returned to the Friendly Arm Inn. I should go back and speak to her.~
